# Milestone: v0.10.10-job-introspection
# Covers: scopeTag builtin returns the implicit scope tag for the current
#         function call; used with every() to auto-cancel a loop when
#         function exits.
# blocked: a function's scope tag is not stopped when the function returns, so `t: every(20ms) ...` under `scopeTag()` goes on firing after the call.
#
# Everything below this line predates the re-foundation: it names
# tasks and entry points that no longer exist, and its account of
# what stands in the way has been superseded by the `blocked:` line
# above, which was probed against this branch.  Kept for the
# original urbiscript it carries.
# matrix-row: tag-scopetag
#
# Reason:
#   scopeTag() shipped v0.10.10 (D7-D) as a call-style native (Realm
#   global). The fixture uses legacy bare-name `var t = scopeTag;` which
#   requires the OGET dispatch path to wrap native closures as
#   auto-invoked getters; that bridge defers v1.x (see workspace-root
#   design-risks v0.10.10-A: urbi_vm_dispatch_getter is bytecode-only and
#   segfaults on native closures because proto=NULL). The fixture also
#   uses `every(1s)` reactive looping + `,` separator for concurrent
#   observation over a 3.5s timeline, both requiring the T39 chk driver.
#   Single-strand cousin tests/chk/tag/scope_tag_basic.chk activates at
#   v0.10.10 and exercises the scopeTag feature itself with call-style.
#
# Original urbiscript (activate when T39 chk driver + native-closure OGET land):
# # function f() { var t = scopeTag; t: every(1s) echo("foobar"), sleep(3.5s) }|;
# # f();
# # [00000001] *** foobar
# # ... (see legacy/repos/aldebaran-urbi/tests/2.x/scope-tag.chk)
